00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,330
 The third kind of component that I want to mention

2
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:07,120
 is the content provider. The content provider provides a structure interface

3
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:09,430
 to a set of data such as for example a set

4
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:12,950
 of pictures or media files in general. As we saw earlier,

5
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:16,948
 Android contains an implementation of the SQ Lite Database manager. So,

6
00:00:16,948 --> 00:00:19,829
 very often, apps rely on a SQ Lite database to store

7
00:00:19,829 --> 00:00:22,442
 the data and a provider to give it access to such

8
00:00:22,442 --> 00:00:25,770
 data. In some cases, a provider can be used for accessing

9
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:28,450
 data within an application. In which case the data will

10
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:31,010
 be application data, such as a list of items to be

11
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:34,160
 bought for a shopping list management application. There is a

12
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:37,640
 much more interesting case, though. More generally a provider can be

13
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:40,820
 used by an application also to share data with other

14
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:44,930
 applications. In the case represent here for instance, this content provider

15
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:47,920
 is being accessed by three different application. If you want an

16
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:51,500
 example, a typical one will be an address book, the contact

17
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,950
 app in your smartphone, for instance. The address

18
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:55,950
 book could use a provider to give access to

19
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,440
 the user contacts to other applications such as, for

20
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:01,820
 example, a telephone application, a voice over IP application,

21
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:04,349
 a messaging application, and so on. So in

22
00:01:04,349 --> 00:01:07,040
 this case, all these applications will be able to

23
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:10,590
 access the same data through a common, well-structured interface,

24
00:01:10,590 --> 00:01:10,590
 which is the one provided by the content provider.

